From: ruje0504-2
Subject: [T214] restore GPIO output state before SC7 pinmux replay

Apply after 0006. Enabled only with SWITCH_LITE_SC7=1 on T210B01.
Save the board's running GPIO output/configuration/direction and pin fields
at the last-CPU boundary. After CAR restore, recover output latches before
direction and mux selection. GPIO interrupt configuration and pending status
are left for GpioClx. Reserved pin fields and MMIO holes are not replayed.
The register/field lists come from Switchroot's T210/B01 group definitions,
including LPDR and the eMMC mux extension; clear the eMMC parking fields on
resume as its pinctrl driver does. Locked or failed writes stop resume.
This does not restore PMC pad voltages, device PHYs, or the DSI controller.

References:
https://github.com/CTCaer/switch-l4t-kernel-4.9/blob/2d0059fd3167a8df756de2aa0489d4aa70a9fc15/drivers/pinctrl/tegra/pinctrl-tegra.c#L898
https://github.com/CTCaer/switch-l4t-kernel-4.9/blob/2d0059fd3167a8df756de2aa0489d4aa70a9fc15/drivers/pinctrl/tegra/pinctrl-tegra210.c
https://github.com/CTCaer/switch-l4t-kernel-4.9/blob/2d0059fd3167a8df756de2aa0489d4aa70a9fc15/drivers/gpio/gpio-tegra.c#L490

--- a/plat/nvidia/tegra/soc/t210/platform_t210.mk
